### Attendance Management System — REST Client sample requests
### Requires the "REST Client" VS Code extension (or compatible).
### This file grows across phases as new endpoints land.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5000/api/v1
@accessToken = REPLACE_WITH_ACCESS_TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN_RESPONSE

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### =========================
### AUTH
### =========================

### Register a new employee (role always defaults to "employee")
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jordan Lee",
  "email": "jordan.lee@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!",
  "department": "Engineering"
}

### Login — sets an httpOnly refreshToken cookie and returns an accessToken in the body
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "jordan.lee@example.com",
  "password": "Passw0rd!"
}

### Get current user (paste accessToken from the login response above into @accessToken)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Update own profile
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auth/update-profile
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Jordan A. Lee",
  "department": "Platform Engineering"
}

### Change own password
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/auth/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "oldPassword": "Passw0rd!",
  "newPassword": "NewPassw0rd!"
}

### Refresh access token — reads the httpOnly refreshToken cookie set by /login
### (Run this in a client that persists cookies between requests, e.g. VS Code REST Client does.)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/refresh-token

### Logout — clears the refreshToken cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### =========================
### USERS (admin / manager)
### =========================

### List all users — admin only. Filters: role, department, isActive, search. Paginated.
GET {{baseUrl}}/users?role=employee&page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get my direct reports — manager or admin
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/team
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Get a single user — admin (any), manager (own team only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/REPLACE_WITH_USER_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Update a user — admin only (role, department, manager, isActive)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/REPLACE_WITH_USER_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "manager",
  "department": "Sales",
  "isActive": true
}

### Soft-delete (deactivate) a user — admin only
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/users/REPLACE_WITH_USER_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### RBAC sanity check — an employee token here must get a 403, not a user list
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer REPLACE_WITH_AN_EMPLOYEE_ACCESS_TOKEN

### =========================
### ATTENDANCE
### =========================
### @selfie holds a real base64 JPEG data URL — paste one captured from the browser console:
###   document.querySelector('canvas').toDataURL('image/jpeg', 0.7)
@selfie = data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAQAAAC1HAwCAAAAC0lEQVR42mNk+A8AAQUBAScY42YAAAAASUVORK5CYII=

### Punch in — employee only
POST {{baseUrl}}/attendance/punch-in
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "selfie": "{{selfie}}",
  "latitude": 22.7196,
  "longitude": 75.8577,
  "address": "Indore, MP, India"
}

### Punch out — employee only
POST {{baseUrl}}/attendance/punch-out
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "selfie": "{{selfie}}",
  "latitude": 22.7196,
  "longitude": 75.8577,
  "address": "Indore, MP, India"
}

### Today's attendance for the current user
GET {{baseUrl}}/attendance/today
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### My attendance history — filters: startDate, endDate, workStatus. Paginated.
GET {{baseUrl}}/attendance/my?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Team attendance — manager (own team) or admin
GET {{baseUrl}}/attendance/team?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### All attendance — admin only
GET {{baseUrl}}/attendance/all?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Dashboard summary counts — scoped to caller's role
GET {{baseUrl}}/attendance/stats/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Single attendance record — scoped (self / own team / any for admin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/attendance/REPLACE_WITH_ATTENDANCE_ID
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Verify (mark valid/invalid) — manager (own team) or admin
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/attendance/REPLACE_WITH_ATTENDANCE_ID/verify
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "verificationStatus": "valid",
  "remarks": "Selfie and location match office premises"
}

### =========================
### OVERTIME
### =========================

### Request overtime — employee only. Only valid for a day with punch-out and >8 worked hours.
POST {{baseUrl}}/overtime
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "attendanceId": "REPLACE_WITH_ATTENDANCE_ID",
  "requestedHours": 1.5,
  "reason": "Closed out a production incident after hours"
}

### My overtime requests — employee
GET {{baseUrl}}/overtime/my?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Pending overtime requests — manager (own team) or admin
GET {{baseUrl}}/overtime/pending?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### All overtime requests — admin only
GET {{baseUrl}}/overtime/all?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Review (approve/reject) — manager (own team) or admin
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/overtime/REPLACE_WITH_OVERTIME_ID/review
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "approved",
  "reviewComment": "Approved — confirmed against the incident timeline"
}

### =========================
### REPORTS
### =========================

### Daily report — scoped. Defaults to today if ?date= is omitted.
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/daily?date=2026-08-07
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Range report — scoped. startDate/endDate required; optional userId (must be within scope).
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/range?startDate=2026-08-01&endDate=2026-08-07
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Export Excel — accepts the same ?date= or ?startDate=&endDate= as above
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/export/excel?date=2026-08-07
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Export PDF — accepts the same ?date= or ?startDate=&endDate= as above
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/export/pdf?date=2026-08-07
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### =========================
### NOTIFICATIONS
### =========================
### Created automatically when an overtime request is reviewed or an attendance record is
### verified — delivered instantly over Socket.IO to the affected user, and listed here too.

### My notifications (includes unreadCount)
GET {{baseUrl}}/notifications?page=1&limit=10
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Mark one notification as read
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notifications/REPLACE_WITH_NOTIFICATION_ID/read
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Mark all notifications as read
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/notifications/read-all
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
